1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Be7 5. e3 O-O 6. Nf3 h6 7. Bh4 Nbd7 8. Bd3
c5 9. O-O cxd4 10. exd4 {I felt that when I have IQP I should try to fight for
initiative and start an attack} 10... dxc4 11. Bxc4 Nb6 12. Bd3 (12. Bb3
{definitely a better move than Bd3 as it is more flexible. This move supports
the d5 break and Bb3 might go to c2 and make battery with Qd3}) 12... Nbd5 13.
Qd2 b6 14. Ne5 Bb7 15. a3 {I thought black might play Bb4 and Rc8, I felt this
pin is very irritating and a3 also stops Nb4} 15... Rc8 16. f4 {This move helps
with the in the attack but is also a weakening move as now light squares are
very weak} 16... Nxc3 17. bxc3 Ne4 {My opponent immediately punished me} 18.
Bxe4 Bxe4 19. Bxe7 Qxe7 ∓ {Black is already better as the bishop is just better
than my knight as the bishop controls a lot of squares and my Ne5 can be easily
kick out with f6} 20. a4 Qc7 21. Ra3 {I wanted to create some counter play} (21.
Rae1 {is better as the rook lift(Re3 to Rg3) would have helped in the attack})
21... Rfd8 22. Qe3 Qb7 23. Qg3 Rd5 24. Qh4 {I spent 14 minutes on this move,
trying to find a way to continue the attack so I thought to play c4 and slide my
rook to g3 but I completely missed the next move} 24... Bxg2!! {[%c_effect
g2;square;g2;type;Brilliant;persistent;true]} 25. Rd1 {I am still trying to play
c4 by protecting the d-pawn} 25... Rdd8 26. c4 Be4 ({If any other move like
this} 26... Rf8 {would lead white to have compensation and a decisive attack by
playing the only move} 27. Rg3) 27. Rg3 Kh7 28. Kf2 f6 -+ 29. Rdg1 {Just trying
to put pressure on the black king} 29... fxe5 30. Rxg7+ Qxg7 31. Rxg7+ Kxg7 32.
Qe7+ Kh8 33. Qf6+ Kh7 34. Qf7+ Kh8 35. Qf6+ Kh7 36. Qf7+ 1/2-1/2

